# Environment variables for the Rosica site.
#
# Set these in the Vercel project (Settings -> Environment Variables), then
# redeploy — variables only reach a *new* build, never the running one.
#
# Never commit real values. This file is the template only.


# Search engine indexing.
#
# Off unless this is exactly "true". Leave it off while any page is still a
# placeholder — thin pages indexed early take a long time to undo. Turning it
# on fills the sitemap, opens robots.txt and drops the noindex tags.

ALLOW_INDEXING=


# The Rosica assistant (the chat widget).
#
# Optional, and the only variable the site needs. Without it the chat launcher
# simply never appears — no broken button, the site is otherwise unchanged.
# With it, /api/chat answers visitors from a brief built out of the site's own
# content, so it cannot invent product or ingredient claims.
#
# Get a key at https://console.anthropic.com -> API keys -> Create key.
# Set a monthly spend limit while you are there: the widget is open to anyone
# who loads the page.

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=


# The Shopify store, for live prices and the bag.
#
# Both are needed together. Without them the bag, the Add to Bag buttons and
# every price disappear, and the Buy Now buttons fall back to plain links to
# the store — the site is exactly as it was before the store existed.
#
# The token is the *public* Storefront access token from the Headless sales
# channel (Sales channels -> Headless -> your storefront -> Storefront API).
# Shopify designs it to be readable in browser code, so it is not a secret in
# the way an API key is — but it still lives here, never in the repo, so that
# rotating it is a redeploy rather than a search.

SHOPIFY_STORE_DOMAIN=
SHOPIFY_STOREFRONT_TOKEN=


# There is deliberately no mail configuration here.
#
# The contact page asks visitors to email info@rosica.ae directly rather than
# posting a form, so the site never needs a mailbox credential and there is
# nothing to break when one expires. If a real contact form is wanted later,
# the previous implementation — a route, an SMTP/Resend transport and an
# automatic acknowledgement — is in the git history and can be restored.
